  "sources": [
    "symbol and footprint from an EasyEDA user library (C9900187880) – not orderable; the Nano is plugged in",
    "pin numbers: Arduino Nano numbering (1 = D1/TX … 30 = VIN); matches the EasyEDA symbol (schematic create, 2026-10-25)",
    "ATmega328P: VIH ≥ 0.6 × VCC, VIL ≤ 0.3 × VCC (datasheet, DC characteristics); 16 MHz from about 3.8 V (safe operating area)",
    "5V pin on USB power = VBUS minus a Schottky diode (MBR0520) – source in hardware/sim.json",
    "3V3 pin: from the FT232RL on the original (max. 50 mA), from the CH340's V3 on clones – load not specified, 10 mA assumed; unused here (D-4)",
    "20 mA per GPIO recommended (40 mA absolute maximum)",
    "footprint COMM-TH_L43.2-W17.8-P2.54_ATMEGA328P (2026-10-25): 30 pads Ø1.7 mm, holes 1.1 mm – replaces COMM-TH_ARDUINO_NANO (0.9 mm holes, L-9 failed, D-7); same pad numbering, turned by 90°",
    "pin names as in the EasyEDA symbol (ATmega port names). The symbol labels pin 14 'PB4' and pin 15 'PB3'; on the Nano pin 14 is D11 = PB3 and pin 15 is D12 = PB4. Only the labels are swapped: the footprint's pad 15 sits at the end of the row, where the Nano has D12 (checked after placing). Connections go by pin number, so U1.14 = D11, U1.15 = D12 as the firmware expects.",
    "print per pin: the labels of Arduino's pinout page (A000005-full-pinout.pdf, last update 30/06/2021, https://docs.arduino.cc/resources/pinouts/A000005-full-pinout.pdf) – ~ marks a PWM pin – taken from edakit's library entry A000005 by pin number (D-31); pin 14 prints ~D11 and pin 15 D12 although the EasyEDA symbol names them PB4/PB3 (D-7)"
  ],
